# Packages/Sentinel — corrected AIDE run, 2026-09-03
#
# The run that proves the --config fix, and that produced the 900s timeout
# finding. Executed by hand, not through the sweep, because the fix was still
# being written when it started.
#
# Command: aide --config /etc/aide/aide.conf --check
# Host identifiers redacted.

## <host-a> — 88,000-entry host
exit=7   (1 new | 2 removed | 4 changed, OR'd)
  Total number of entries:  87854
  Added entries:            27
  Removed entries:          18
  Changed entries:          1843

  Changed, grouped by path:
    995  /usr/share      206  /usr/bin       183  /var/lib
    182  /usr/lib         47  /usr/sbin       34  /run/user
      6  /etc/pam.d        6  /run/docker      5  /run/systemd
  -> 1774 of 1843 under /usr (package-owned paths)

  Removed entries are the superseded bind9 libraries:
    libdns-9.20.24-1ubuntu0.2-Ubuntu.so   (upgraded to 1ubuntu0.3)
    libisc / libisccc / libisccfg / libns  same version bump
    + rotated dpkg backup files, + ephemeral journal stream sockets

  ATTRIBUTION: unattended-upgrades ran 2026-09-02 06:07 and replaced
  util-linux, login, diffutils, gnu-coreutils, openssl, bind9, zlib, cpio.
  The AIDE baseline was taken 2026-09-01. debsums exited 0 on the same host
  in the same window -- every packaged file matches the distribution's own
  checksum. The deltas are a distribution upgrade, corroborated three ways.

## <host-b> — 132,000-entry host
exit=7
  Total number of entries:  132038
  Added entries:            54
  Removed entries:          14
  Changed entries:          3502

  Changed, grouped by path:
    2973  /usr/share      255  /opt/<app>      118  /usr/lib
      92  /var/lib         14  /run/systemd     13  /usr/bin

  ATTRIBUTION, two distinct causes:
    a) /usr/*  -- unattended-upgrades ran 2026-09-01 06:38 (util-linux, bind9,
       coreutils, libattr1, libssh, zlib). debsums exits 0 on this host: every
       packaged file matches the distribution's checksum.
    b) /opt/<app> (255 changed, plus most of the 54 added and 14 removed) --
       the application's OWN live data: rotated backups, daily logs, per-player
       plugin state, profiler temp files. This directory changes continuously by
       design and is NOT excluded from the AIDE config.

  TUNING GAP: watching an application's live data directory guarantees hundreds
  of "changes" per day forever. Same class as the container-image-layer exclusion
  already applied on <host-a>, which cut that baseline from 846,423 entries to
  87,847. This one has not been done.

  TIMING: this walk ran ~1,100s+ and the 900s ssh session timeout fired first;
  the remote process survived it, which is the only reason a result exists.
  -> KNOWN_ISSUES.md#the-runner-s-fixed-900-second-command-ti_b1115836
  -> DEFAULT_TIMEOUT raised 900 -> 3600, per-host override, timeout given its
     own verdict so a slow check never again reads as an unreachable host.

## What this run establishes about the TOOL
  1. --config fix works: AIDE executed and returned a real verdict (exit 7),
     where the sweep of the same day returned exit 17 having checked nothing.
  2. 900s was too short, measured rather than guessed this time.
  3. The classifier's bitmask decode was correct on real output: exit 7
     decomposes to new + removed + changed, and all three were present.
